# Server
PORT=3001
# NODE_ENV=production

# CORS: allowed origins are derived automatically
# (localhost / 127.0.0.1, *.vercel.app, *.railway.app). No extra env var needed.
#
# To restrict to a specific production frontend, set CORS_ORIGINS (comma
# separated). It is merged with the automatic allow-list.
# CORS_ORIGINS=https://your-frontend.vercel.app

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cookies / SameSite
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SameSite policy for the refresh + CSRF cookies.
#   - "lax"  (local dev default / same-site proxy): most restrictive.
#   - "none" (production default here): required when the frontend and backend
#     are on SEPARATE sites. Railway's default `*.up.railway.app` domains are
#     each their own site (public suffix), so SameSite=Lax cookies are not sent
#     on cross-site fetch requests. Requires Secure (HTTPS), auto-set in prod.
# CSRF remains protected by the double-submit token (cookie + X-CSRF-Token).
# COOKIE_SAMESITE=none

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Media processing (video tools)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Absolute path to the ffmpeg binary. On Railway (Dockerfile installs ffmpeg)
# this can stay unset and "ffmpeg" from PATH is used.
# FFMPEG_PATH=/usr/bin/ffmpeg

# Hard timeout for a single FFmpeg invocation, in milliseconds.
# FFMPEG_TIMEOUT_MS=900000

# Maximum accepted video upload size, in megabytes.
# MAX_VIDEO_SIZE_MB=100

# How long finished jobs (and their output files) are kept for download,
# in minutes. Orphaned temp dirs are swept with the same TTL.
# MEDIA_JOB_TTL_MINUTES=30

# Maximum number of FFmpeg jobs running at the same time.
# MAX_CONCURRENT_MEDIA_JOBS=6

# Where per-job working directories are created. Defaults to <dist>/temp/media.
# Point this at a persistent volume with enough headroom for ~3x the largest upload.
# MEDIA_TEMP_DIR=/data/media-temp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PostgreSQL (Morven Connect)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Railway: create a PostgreSQL plugin and use its connection string here.
# The schema is PostgreSQL (prisma/schema.prisma). Do not use SQLite.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/morven_connect?schema=public

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# JWT Authentication
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both secrets are REQUIRED at runtime (the app refuses to start without them).
# Generate with e.g. `openssl rand -hex 64`.
# JWT_SECRET=<random-64-char-hex-string>
# JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=<random-64-char-hex-string>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Sign-In (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Google OAuth 2.0 Web Client ID. Used as the `audience` when verifying
# Google ID tokens on POST /api/auth/google. Only required if Google Sign-In
# is enabled. Create one at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# (OAuth client ID, "Web application"). Never commit the real value.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=<your-web-client-id>.apps.googleusercontent.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Speech-to-text (Whisper) model cache
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model cache directory. Defaults to <project>/.models; mounted at /app/.models
# in the Docker image. The image preloads the model at build time where possible,
# otherwise it is fetched on first use (needs outbound access to huggingface.co).
# HF_HOME=/app/.models
# STT_MODEL=Xenova/whisper-base

# Strict rate limit (requests / 15 min) for the password-reset endpoints
# (/api/auth/forgot-password and /api/auth/reset-password). Set low to block
# enumeration/credential-stuffing. Increase for local testing.
# RESET_RATE_LIMIT_MAX=5

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Password reset (email via Resend)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED for the forgot/reset-password feature.
# - RESEND_API_KEY: your Resend API key (https://resend.com). Never commit it.
# - EMAIL_FROM: the "from" address, a verified sender in Resend.
#   e.g. "Morven <no-reply@yourdomain.com>"
# - PUBLIC_BASE_URL: absolute origin of the FRONTEND (used to build the reset
#   link). Server-side only — never taken from the client.
# - PASSWORD_RESET_TOKEN_TTL_MINUTES: reset link validity (default 60).
# For tests set EMAIL_TRANSPORT=mock to disable real sending (no key needed).
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# EMAIL_FROM=Morven <no-reply@yourdomain.com>
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://your-frontend.vercel.app
# PASSWORD_RESET_TOKEN_TTL_MINUTES=60
# EMAIL_TRANSPORT=mock

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uploads persistence (Runtime volume)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uploaded images/avatars/media are stored under <dist>/uploads (= /app/uploads
# in the container). Mount a Railway Volume at /app/uploads so uploads survive
# redeploys and restarts.
# RUNTIME_VOLUME=/app/uploads
